.TH STREAMLINE-INDEX 1 "Jan 2026" "streamline-vectors" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
streamline-index \- build search index for Streamline icons
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B streamline-index
.RI [ DATA_DIR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B streamline-index
builds an SQLite database index for the Streamline icon collection to enable
fast searching. The index includes structured information about each icon's
category, style (if applicable), subcategory, and filename.
.PP
The indexing process parses the directory structure to extract:
.TP
.B Categories
Main organizational groups (plump, core, flex, sharp, ultimate, block, etc.)
.TP
.B Styles
Visual style variants (duo, flat, gradient, solid, etc.) for applicable categories
.TP
.B Subcategories
Functional groupings (culture, arrows, interface-essential, leisure/drink-food, etc.)
.TP
.B Filenames
Icon names without the .svg extension
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -c, --content
Extract content from SVG files (titles, descriptions, etc.) for full-text search.
This makes indexing slower but enables searching within SVG content.
.TP
.B -r, --recursive
Recursively index all subdirectories. This is the default when no specific
files or directories are provided.
.TP
.B -f, --force
Overwrite existing index file without prompting.
.TP
.B -o, --output FILE
Specify output path for the index database file.
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Decrease verbosity. Can be used multiple times.
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Increase verbosity. Can be used multiple times.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.I FILES/DIR...
Files and directories to index. If none specified, indexes all icons in the
default data directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STREAMLINE_DATA_DIR
Path to the icon data directory (default: /usr/share/streamline-vectors)
.TP
.B STREAMLINE_INDEX
Path where the index database will be created (default: /var/lib/streamline-vectors/index.db)
.TP
.B STREAMLINE_INDEX_CONTENT
Set to "1" to extract and index SVG content (titles, descriptions, etc.) - slower but more comprehensive
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Build index with default settings:
.B streamline-index
.TP
Build index for custom data directory:
.B streamline-index /path/to/icons
.TP
Build index with content extraction:
.B STREAMLINE_INDEX_CONTENT=1 streamline-index
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/streamline-vectors/index.db
SQLite search index database (output)
.TP
.I /usr/share/streamline-vectors/
Icon data directory (input)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR streamline-find (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1)
